    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only concrete test class (the others are a base and a helper). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on `POST /api/owners` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the new owner's firstName + lastName (case-insensitively) at creation time, persisted and returned on subsequent GETs.\n\nChanges:\n- **`CountNamesakes.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners matching firstName+lastName (trimmed, lower-cased) via `ownerRepository.findAll()` before the new owner is saved, and sets it on the built owner in place.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the `countNamesakes` step in (under `transaction` governance) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`, so it runs before persistence.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` read-only int32 property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n- **Schema DDL** (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) \u2014 added the `namesake_count INTEGER` column.\n- **hsqldb `data.sql`** \u2014 the seed owner rows use positional inserts, so I appended a `NULL` for the new column (the other dialects use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe `coreCountsNamesakes` acceptance test (two owners sharing \"Ann\" + surname \u2192 second owner reports `namesakeCount = 1`) and the full suite pass green.",
